Introduction
Imagine waking up and discovering that the Internet has disappeared.
You can't message friends, watch videos, use online banking, play online games, attend online classes, or access cloud storage.
Nearly everything we do today depends on one invisible system:
Computer networks.
A computer network allows devices to exchange information. It is the foundation of cybersecurity, cloud computing, artificial intelligence, online gaming, banking, healthcare, education, and modern businesses.
If computers were people, a network would be the roads that allow everyone to communicate.
Without roads, cities cannot function.
Without networks, computers become isolated.
________________________________________
Why Do Networks Exist?
Early computers worked alone.
If someone wanted to share information, they often had to physically move storage devices between computers.
As organizations grew, this became slow and inefficient.
Networking solved this problem by allowing computers to communicate instantly.
Today, billions of devices exchange information every second.
