How Does a Network Work?
Suppose you send a photo to a friend.
The process looks like this:
Your Phone
      │
      ▼
 Wi-Fi Router
      │
      ▼
 Internet
      │
      ▼
 Friend's Internet Provider
      │
      ▼
 Friend's Router
      │
      ▼
 Friend's Phone
The photo is broken into many small pieces called packets.
Each packet travels through the network and is reassembled at the destination.
You'll study packets in detail in later chapters.
