Core Concepts
Communication
Networks exist to enable communication.
Examples:
•	Video calls
•	Online games
•	Email
•	Messaging
________________________________________
Resource Sharing
Instead of buying one printer for every employee, an office can connect one printer to the network.
Everyone can use it.
Other shared resources include:
•	Internet access
•	Storage
•	Databases
•	Applications
________________________________________
Reliability
Modern networks are designed so communication can continue even if one connection fails.
This is called redundancy, and you'll learn more about it in advanced chapters.
________________________________________
Scalability
A good network should grow without requiring a complete redesign.
For example:
•	A home network may have 10 devices.
•	A university may have 20,000 devices.
•	A cloud provider may have millions of servers.
The same networking principles apply, but the design becomes more sophisticated.
