Lab Practice
Lab 1: Explore Your Home Network
Objective
Identify the devices already connected to your network.
Requirements
•	A Windows, Linux, or macOS computer.
•	Access to your home Wi-Fi.
Steps
1.	Connect your computer to your network.
2.	Open a command prompt or terminal.
3.	Run:
o	Windows: ipconfig
o	Linux/macOS: ip addr
4.	Record:
o	Your IP address
o	Default gateway
o	DNS server
5.	Log in to your router (if you have permission) and compare the information with what your computer reports.
Expected Outcome
You can identify your own device's network settings and understand that your router assigns or helps manage network connectivity.
Challenge
Count how many devices are connected to your network and identify which are computers, phones, TVs, printers, or IoT devices.
