Common Mistakes
•	Thinking the Internet and the Web are the same thing.
•	Assuming Wi-Fi is the Internet (Wi-Fi is only one way to connect to a network).
•	Believing every network requires Internet access (many private networks do not).
•	Thinking routers and switches perform the same job.
