Frequently Asked Questions
Q: Is Wi-Fi the Internet?
No. Wi-Fi is a wireless method of connecting to a network. The Internet is a global network of networks.
Q: Can a network exist without Internet access?
Yes. Many home, office, and laboratory networks operate without being connected to the Internet.
Q: Why do cybersecurity professionals need networking?
Because almost every cyberattack and defense involves devices communicating across a network.
